Appendix I — Open Problems and Research Directions

I.1 Open Theoretical Problems

Problem I.1 (Dynamic DV zero characterization). Characterize the histories at which dynamic DV is zero. This is strictly stronger than Theorem 4.1.

Problem I.2 (Reservation-value stopping). Prove or refute Conjecture 7.1 under regularity conditions on F_i^{(1)},F_i^{(0)}.

Problem I.3 (Sub-optimality of fixed-order). Exhibit a concrete n-candidate instance where the optimal adaptive policy strictly dominates every fixed-order committed policy.

Problem I.4 (State-dependent budget). Under Hypothesis 8.1, is the optimal budget \tau^\star state-dependent?

Problem I.5 (Complementarity under resource dependence). Does resource dependence create new complementarities absent from the fixed-\epsilon model?

Problem I.6 (Treewidth bound). Is there a treewidth-based upper bound on the computational value of verification for Lean proof-search AND/OR graphs?

Problem I.7 (Krajíček bridge). Is there a connection between proof complexity lower bounds and the decision value of verification?

I.2 Future Empirical Directions (Not in This Paper)

· Calibration of F_i^{(1)},F_i^{(0)} against Lean heartbeat statistics.
· Numerical comparison of fixed-order and adaptive policies for n\le6.
· Test of Conjecture 7.1 via exhaustive enumeration.

